{#
  Section: owns the macro rhythm. Vertical padding (the section-level step of
  the spacing scale, and the ONLY place that step is allowed, never
  component-internal) plus the 1120px container, both applied automatically.

  py-22 is Tailwind's 88px step, the section rhythm this site was reset to when
  the above-title was retired. The container it wraps is .cs-container, not
  max-w-main plus px-8; see components/container.css for why.

  IT WAS py-24, 96px, UNTIL 2026-08-19, and it moved through a temporary `pad`
  argument rather than in one edit. Five pages call this macro, so flipping the
  default is a five-page change, and the first page was reset on its own so a
  mistake would have been one page's mistake. Every caller has now moved and the
  argument is gone, which is what it was there to allow.

  It had to be an argument rather than a page-level CSS override: this is a
  Tailwind utility, and utilities sit in a later cascade layer than
  @layer components, so a page stylesheet cannot beat it. That override looks
  like it works until someone reads the computed value.

  `deep` paints the one ink pane. design.md section 1: MAX ONE deep pane per
  view. Buttons inside a deep section must use variant="deep", and the wordmark
  its --on-deep modifier, or they render ink-on-ink and vanish.

  Usage:
    {% raw %}{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
    {% call section(deep=true) %}...{% endcall %}{% endraw %}
#}
{#- `orient` names this section for the masthead's left slot, on the <section>
    that already exists rather than on a marker element. See container.njk. -#}
{% macro section(deep=false, class="", containerClass="", id="", label="", orient="") %}
<section{% if id %} id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}{% if label %} aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}{% if orient %} data-orient="{{ orient }}"{% endif %} class="py-22{{ " bg-ink text-paper" if deep }}{{ " " + class if class }}">
  <div class="cs-container{{ " " + containerClass if containerClass }}">
    {{ caller() }}
  </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
